[1mPhase C writeup.[22m [38;5;10mtranslation/ERRORS.md[0m records the verification rather than a list of repairs, since there were none. It documents each risk area above, the sweep counts, the mutation results, and six branches in the C that [1mno input can reach[22m — XOR's [38;5;10mreturn 90[0m, NAND's [38;5;10mreturn 100[0m, [38;5;10mvalidate_sequence[0m's [38;5;10mreturn 40[0m (Rule 3 already forces [38;5;10mtransitions >= 3[0m when [38;5;10mlen > 10[0m), the [38;5;10mread && write[0m fall-through, the two [38;5;10mconfigure_flags[0m search-loop exits, and the [38;5;10mNULL[0m guard. Those are dead in the source, not gaps in the suite, so I recorded the reasoning instead of leaving them looking untested.[0m[0m
